1. SIBLING PARITY
   The switch's three siblings (MACPPC +0x160, HPCMIPS guarded absolute, IQ80321 +0x402) have
   NO detector in this tree.  The new case is the only one rowed.  N/A as an asymmetry to repair:
   this round adds one case, and rowing machines with no rig is outside it.  Disclosed below.

2. CLAIM -> ROW  (every added comment sentence asserting an observable consequence)
   "the kernel writes Device Control at 0x2c"      -> `aux 2c reset' (the write reaches the device)
   "a soft reset that lands purges the ring"         -> `aux 2c reset' 0x09 -> 0x01; `live' proves the
                                                        ring is live (0x09) when no reset lands
   "0x206 is no longer mapped on landisk"            -> `aux 206 gone', `206 ctl dead'
   "delivers nIEN, does not implement it"            -> NO ROW, deliberately: an unimplemented bit has
                                                        no observable to pin.  Stated in the contract.

3. GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD
   Guard: `devinit->machine->machine_type' (the case label).  Body: `devinit->addr' plus a constant.
   The two are set at construction and never re-written, so no third state exists in which they
   disagree.  N/A, reason recorded.

